Design Robinhood's fractional share buying feature. Users can place a dollar-denominated order (e.g. "buy $10 of AAPL") instead of a whole-share order. Since exchanges only trade whole shares, the system must pool many users' fractional orders together, execute whole-share market orders on their behalf, and then allocate each resulting fill back to the individual users pro-rata to their requested dollar amount, even as prices move between order pooling and execution.
